*.tgz
*.zip
.sixth/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# ── Local agent context (see ARCHITECTURE.md for the public architecture reference) ──
# CLAUDE.md aggregates the live host, credentials, testing toggles and the full weakness list in
# one file. Useful locally, unwise to publish.
CLAUDE.md

# ── Post-submission divergence record (local only) ──
# Tracks where the frozen capstone paper disagrees with the current code. Deliberately NOT published:
# it enumerates each security hole that was closed, and the CCSCloud VM still runs the pre-fix
# chaincode, so publishing it would be a roadmap to an unpatched host. Personal reference.
docs/submission/cap2/references/CAP2 - Post-Submission Changes*

# ── CAP1 submitted PDFs ──
# The originally submitted CAP1 manuals. WALKTHROUGH.pdf carries the full demo-account table with
# live passwords; INSTALLATION, TECHNICAL and Defense Knowledge carry the CouchDB admin credentials.
# The readable .md mirrors alongside them stay tracked, so nothing of substance is lost by excluding
# the PDFs. Keep the local copies — these are the formal submission record.
docs/submission/cap1/*.pdf
